# ============================================================
#  Templates (docs/grimoire-script.md §9).
#  A thread with `params:` is a template: a thread `from:` it fills the params in (`with:`), lists its cards by role
#  (`members:`), and each member takes its role's pool (<template>.<role>) and may call the template's presets
#  (<template>.<name>, or just <name>). Pools here that other pools build on (`from:`) hold what a kind of pool shares.
#  Macros inside a template: $param, $this (the card), $thread, $<role> (a role's only card), a member's own values
#  ($flag), count(<role>: expr) and `first <role> [except this] [where expr]:`.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- story: a start card, then steps that wait on what it began ----------------

@thread story
desc: A bespoke storyline. The start card begins it (it sets what $begun tests); every other card is a step and waits on $begun.
params: begun
roles: start step
default_role: step

@pool story.step
when: $begun

# ---------------- quest: start, preparations in any order, a final check (every club and job capstone) ----------------

@thread quest
desc: A start card offers it once ($begun not yet set); the parts come in any order, each until its $flag is set; the final needs $need parts $after month(s) after the start, or comes anyway $giveup months on. `next` (in a part's working option) deals, once a day ($beat), the final when it is ready, else the next part not done.
params: begun need=2 after=1 giveup=4 beat=chain_beat
roles: start part final

@pool quest.start
trigger: auto
repeat: 3
when: not flag($begun)

@pool quest.part
repeat: 2
weight: 60
when: flag($begun) and not flag($flag)

@pool quest.final
class: milestone
repeat: 2
weight: 40
when: flag($begun) and since($start) >= $after and (count(part: flag($flag)) >= $need or since($start) >= $giveup)

@preset quest.next
desc: Once a day: the final if enough parts are done, else the next part not done (this one aside).
do:
  if $beat != turn:
    $beat = turn
    if since($start) >= $after and count(part: flag($flag)) >= $need:
      queue $final now
    else:
      first part except this where not flag($flag):
        queue $part now

# ---------------- scene: a run of cards in one sitting ----------------

@thread scene
desc: A run of cards in one visit. Entry cards start it; each step that is got past deals the next with `next`, drawn from the scene's queued cards like any pool.
roles: entry step
default_role: step

@pool scene.step
trigger: queued

@preset scene.next
desc: The next card of the scene, drawn from its steps.
do:
  queue any in $thread now

# ---------------- pool templates: what every pool of one kind shares ----------------

@pool course_routine
desc: What every course pool shares (6 pools).
class: routine
repeat: 5
weight: 10
tags: class

@pool course_routine_repeat4
desc: What the course pools whose cards come back four times share (3 pools); the others use course_routine.
class: routine
repeat: 4
weight: 10
tags: class
